## 4. Orchestration Model

### 4.1 Metadata-Centric Orchestrator

[core/orchestrator.py](../core/orchestrator.py) remains the metadata coordination layer:

- Session context lifecycle.
- Schema/target aggregation semantics.
- Non-heavyweight orchestration decisions.

### 4.2 Execution Orchestrator

[pipeline/training_orchestrator.py](../pipeline/training_orchestrator.py) is the execution-phase engine:

- Data ingest registration/use.
- Preprocessing execution.
- Model selection and Optuna training.
- Drift detection and retraining trigger path.
- Model registry output.

### 4.3 State and Session Persistence

- [core/execution_context.py](../core/execution_context.py) defines ExecutionContext and session metadata fields.
- [database/context_db.py](../database/context_db.py) persists session context and dataset profiles.
- Context DB now sets:
  - PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL
  - PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000

